<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donald Cameron (colonial administrator)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1872">1872</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Donald Charles Cameron (1872–1948) was a British colonial administrator who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-territory">Tanganyika Territory</a> from 1925 to 1931 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> from 1931 to 1935. In Tanganyika he introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a> through chiefs and native authorities, modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Lugard</a>'s system in Nigeria, and set up the territory's Legislative Council in 1926.</p></div>
